From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 21:05:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/arkweb: Wire touch, scroll and key input; fix
 open/close leaks

Translate ACE touch/scroll/key events into servo InputEvents:
- touch tap/drag -> InputEvent::Touch (servo derives scroll from the
  sequence). ACE forwards touch-move through the batched
  OnTouchMove(vector<NWebTouchPointInfo>) overload, so override it or
  drags are dropped.
- key input via SendKeyboardEvent (the path this ACE version uses),
  mapping the OHOS keycode/unicode to a servo Key. A key dispatched before the
  engine is running is reported as unhandled, so ACE falls back to its own key
  handling instead of assuming we consumed the event.
- ExecuteJavaScript wired fire-and-forget.

Fix the open/close leaks: release the OHNativeWindow from
CreateNativeWindowFromSurface on destroy, and hold the nwebs_ map as
weak_ptr so a destroyed component's NWeb and its handler proxy are freed.

License the port as Apache-2.0 and ignore it in servo-tidy.

Validation: Test by running uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_scroll.py on a device; key input is covered by test_ime.py.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <jschwender@posteo.net>
